layout_spec.add_channel_button:
A half-size 16:9 Glass PANEL button, right of the centred bottom picture and centred on it vertically:
- width = min(ADD_SCALE*cw, w - gap - (bottom.right + gap)) = min(232, 236) = 232 dp;
- height = width*9/16 = 130.5 dp;
- left = bottom.right + gap = 718 dp;
- top = bottom.top + (ch - height)/2 = 338.25 dp.
Box(718, 338.25, 232, 130.5) dp = 464x261 px at (1436,677), spanning to (1900,938); 20 px from the right edge, 12 px from the bottom picture.
It keeps today's content: the 30 dp + icon and the 15 sp 'Add a channel' label, with a 10 dp gap (about 60 dp tall in a 130.5 dp box). Its corners stay at the panel radius (radius_panel 15 dp), so the white ring hugs them.
MultiviewBoard needs no logic change: place() already sizes, places and fades the Add cell from layout.add (MultiviewBoard.kt:291-309).
D-pad (MultiviewLayout.move, checked by hand on these boxes):
- top-right Down -> Add;
- top-left Down -> bottom;
- bottom Right -> Add;
- Add Left -> bottom;
- Add Up -> top-right;
- bottom Left -> top-left.
Bottom Up is an exact tie between the two top pictures. move() gets a tolerance (score < bestScore - 0.5f) so a tie always goes to the earlier picture (top-left). The same rule fixes the tie Down from the large picture onto two small ones.

