verdicts.issues:
All the maths checks out at 960x540 dp, gap 6:
- grid cell 464x261, left 13, top 6;
- bottom picture centred at 248 (right edge 712);
- Add min(232, 236) = 232 x 130.5 at (718, 338.25); the 4th edge is 950 <= 954;
- 70.1% / 5.8% and 93.4% are correct; two tiles cover 48.1% (not 48.2%);
- every listed D-pad result is correct, and assertSane passes with Add.
Problems:
(1) The TIE tolerance is unnecessary and its stated reason is wrong. move() already uses a strict 'score < bestScore', so an exact tie already goes to the earlier stop. MultiviewRulesTest's downFromTheLargePictureLandsOnTheSmallOneUnderIt already asserts 'Two small ones the same distance away: the first'.
(2) 3->4 now overlaps. place() settles a new picture at once (MultiviewBoard 288-289) while the centred bottom picture slides from 496..1424 px to 26..954 px, across the new 4th's surface at 966.. for 260 ms. Sibling SurfaceViews have no defined order, so they flicker. In the old grid nothing moved on 3->4. mv-polish item 1 fixes this but is only 'could'.
(3) 'Bottom-left slides to the centre' on 4->3 holds only when the 4th picture is removed. Removing picture 0 moves old 2 to the top right and old 3 to the centre.
(4) 'Diagonal inset 7.0 -> 4.7 px' is the per-axis offset of the 45-degree point; along the diagonal it is 9.9 -> 6.6 px.
